WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.395
Resume Writing.

2
00:00:01.675 --> 00:00:05.281
Day 80 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Career phase.

3
00:00:07.031 --> 00:00:08.055
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.335 --> 00:00:18.895
Today's goal: write a clear, one-to-two-page resume (CV) that shows results, passes applicant tracking systems (ATS), and makes a recruiter want to call you.

5
00:00:20.245 --> 00:00:21.098
Part 1.

6
00:00:21.378 --> 00:00:22.679
How resumes are read.

7
00:00:23.929 --> 00:00:32.761
A recruiter often spends under a minute on the first look, and many companies first filter resumes with an ATS (software that matches keywords).

8
00:00:33.041 --> 00:00:38.225
So your resume must be easy to scan and use the same words as the job description.

9
00:00:39.575 --> 00:00:40.493
Step 1:

10
00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:44.911
Header: name, phone, email, city, LinkedIn, GitHub or portfolio.

11
00:00:45.191 --> 00:00:46.109
Step 2:

12
00:00:46.389 --> 00:00:47.157
Summary:

13
00:00:47.437 --> 00:00:50.615
2 to 3 lines: who you are, your strengths, what you want.

14
00:00:50.895 --> 00:00:51.813
Step 3:

15
00:00:52.093 --> 00:00:55.591
Skills: grouped: languages, frameworks, cloud, tools.

16
00:00:55.871 --> 00:00:56.831
Step 4:

17
00:00:57.111 --> 00:01:01.207
Experience: newest first; 3 to 5 result bullets per role.

18
00:01:01.487 --> 00:01:02.447
Step 5:

19
00:01:02.727 --> 00:01:06.717
Projects, education, certifications: the most relevant only.

20
00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:08.941
Part 2.

21
00:01:09.221 --> 00:01:10.395
Length and format.

22
00:01:11.645 --> 00:01:12.989
Here is a quick table:

23
00:01:13.269 --> 00:01:14.741
Experience, and Length.

24
00:01:15.021 --> 00:01:17.026
Fresher or 0 to 3 years:

25
00:01:17.306 --> 00:01:18.159
1 page.

26
00:01:18.439 --> 00:01:19.655
3 to 10 years:

27
00:01:19.935 --> 00:01:21.215
1 to 2 pages.

28
00:01:21.495 --> 00:01:22.583
10 plus years:

29
00:01:22.863 --> 00:01:25.743
2 pages (focus on the last 8 to 10 years).

30
00:01:27.093 --> 00:01:35.136
Simple layout, one column, standard fonts, clear headings; avoid tables, images and text boxes (ATS can't read them).

31
00:01:35.416 --> 00:01:39.277
Save as PDF (unless the job asks for Word); file name:

32
00:01:39.557 --> 00:01:42.011
Ashish-Gupta-Backend-Engineer.pdf.

33
00:01:42.291 --> 00:01:49.480
No photo, date of birth, religion, marital status or full address unless the country or company requires them.

34
00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:51.726
Part 3.

35
00:01:52.006 --> 00:01:53.201
The bullet formula.

36
00:01:54.451 --> 00:01:55.795
Here is a quick table:

37
00:01:56.075 --> 00:01:57.803
Weak bullet, and Strong bullet.

38
00:01:58.083 --> 00:02:00.109
Responsible for backend development.:

39
00:02:00.389 --> 00:02:06.469
Built 12 Spring Boot microservices for order and payment flows, handling 2M+ requests a day.

40
00:02:06.749 --> 00:02:08.563
Worked on performance improvement.:

41
00:02:08.843 --> 00:02:18.443
Reduced API p95 latency from 1.4 s to 300 ms by adding Redis caching and fixing N+1 queries.

42
00:02:18.723 --> 00:02:20.579
Did code reviews and mentoring.:

43
00:02:20.859 --> 00:02:24.443
Mentored 4 junior engineers; 2 were promoted within a year.

44
00:02:24.723 --> 00:02:26.067
Handled deployments.:

45
00:02:26.347 --> 00:02:32.768
Automated CI or CD with GitHub Actions, cutting release time from 2 hours to 18 minutes.

46
00:02:34.118 --> 00:02:35.291
No exact number?

47
00:02:35.571 --> 00:02:42.718
Use scale, frequency or comparison: for 40 plus stores, weekly, 3 times faster, first in the team to....

48
00:02:42.998 --> 00:02:52.811
Action verbs: built, designed, led, launched, reduced, improved, automated, migrated, scaled, optimised, delivered, mentored, introduced, resolved.

49
00:02:54.161 --> 00:02:55.079
Part 4.

50
00:02:55.359 --> 00:02:56.788
Summary: examples.

51
00:02:58.038 --> 00:02:59.126
Experienced.

52
00:02:59.406 --> 00:03:01.283
Here is a template you can copy.

53
00:03:01.563 --> 00:03:07.686
Senior Backend Engineer with 9 years building high-scale payment and e-commerce. systems in.

54
00:03:07.966 --> 00:03:10.057
Java, Kafka and AWS.

55
00:03:10.337 --> 00:03:14.710
Led a checkout re-architecture that cut failed orders by 60%.

56
00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:19.043
Looking. for a Staff Engineer role focused on distributed systems.

57
00:03:21.893 --> 00:03:22.725
Fresher.

58
00:03:23.005 --> 00:03:24.883
Here is a template you can copy.

59
00:03:25.163 --> 00:03:30.624
Computer Science graduate (2026) with strong Java and Spring Boot skills.

60
00:03:30.904 --> 00:03:41.293
Built a. grocery. delivery app with 1,000 plus test users as a final-year project and completed a 6-month. backend. internship at XYZ.

61
00:03:41.573 --> 00:03:43.493
Looking for a Software Engineer role.

62
00:03:46.343 --> 00:03:47.453
Career switch.

63
00:03:47.733 --> 00:03:49.610
Here is a template you can copy.

64
00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:56.162
QA engineer moving into backend development, with 4 years of test automation in Java. and.

65
00:03:56.442 --> 00:04:00.687
2 years building internal Spring Boot tools used by 60 engineers.

66
00:04:00.967 --> 00:04:02.482
AWS Certified.

67
00:04:02.762 --> 00:04:03.637
Developer.

68
00:04:06.487 --> 00:04:07.447
Part 5.

69
00:04:07.727 --> 00:04:09.220
Tailor it for each job.

70
00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:13.713
Copy the job description; highlight skills and keywords.

71
00:04:13.993 --> 00:04:18.579
Make sure the same words appear in your summary, skills and bullets (only if true).

72
00:04:18.859 --> 00:04:22.358
Move the most relevant experience and projects to the top.

73
00:04:22.638 --> 00:04:25.219
Remove things that don't help this application.

74
00:04:26.569 --> 00:04:27.508
Part 6.

75
00:04:27.788 --> 00:04:28.897
Common mistakes.

76
00:04:30.147 --> 00:04:31.001
Avoid:

77
00:04:31.281 --> 00:04:34.417
Spelling and grammar errors (ask someone to proofread).

78
00:04:34.697 --> 00:04:35.550
Avoid:

79
00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:38.646
I, me, my in bullets (start with the verb instead).

80
00:04:38.926 --> 00:04:39.779
Avoid:

81
00:04:40.059 --> 00:04:42.022
Long paragraphs instead of bullets.

82
00:04:42.302 --> 00:04:43.155
Avoid:

83
00:04:43.435 --> 00:04:45.910
Listing every technology you've touched once.

84
00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:47.043
Avoid:

85
00:04:47.323 --> 00:04:49.051
Unprofessional email address.

86
00:04:49.331 --> 00:04:50.185
Avoid:

87
00:04:50.465 --> 00:04:54.283
Exaggerating or claiming skills you can't discuss in an interview.

88
00:04:55.633 --> 00:04:56.572
Part 7.

89
00:04:56.852 --> 00:04:59.903
Conversation: getting resume feedback from a senior.

90
00:05:01.153 --> 00:05:03.179
Here is how the conversation goes.

91
00:05:03.459 --> 00:05:06.574
Hi Meena, could you take a quick look at my resume?

92
00:05:06.854 --> 00:05:08.859
I'm applying for senior roles.

93
00:05:09.139 --> 00:05:10.505
Sure, send it over.

94
00:05:10.785 --> 00:05:11.915
Ten minutes later

95
00:05:12.195 --> 00:05:13.454
It's a good start.

96
00:05:13.734 --> 00:05:16.507
But most of your bullets describe duties, not results.

97
00:05:16.787 --> 00:05:18.430
Could you give me an example?

98
00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:21.380
The conversation continues.

99
00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:23.303
Worked on the payment service.

100
00:05:23.583 --> 00:05:25.503
What changed because of your work?

101
00:05:25.783 --> 00:05:34.060
We reduced payment failures from 3% to 0.5% after I added retries and a backup gateway.

102
00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:35.492
That's the bullet!

103
00:05:35.772 --> 00:05:37.095
Put the number in it.

104
00:05:37.375 --> 00:05:38.271
Got it.

105
00:05:38.551 --> 00:05:39.745
Anything else?

106
00:05:41.095 --> 00:05:42.695
The conversation continues.

107
00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:44.789
Your summary is five lines.

108
00:05:45.069 --> 00:05:48.631
Cut it to two or three, and match the keywords in the job description.

109
00:05:48.911 --> 00:05:50.341
That's really helpful.

110
00:05:50.621 --> 00:05:53.714
I'll update it tonight and send you the new version.

111
00:05:55.064 --> 00:05:55.939
Part 8.

112
00:05:56.219 --> 00:05:57.136
Practice.

113
00:05:58.386 --> 00:06:00.306
Rewrite these as result bullets:

114
00:06:00.586 --> 00:06:02.399
Responsible for database work.

115
00:06:02.679 --> 00:06:04.450
Helped in migration to cloud.

116
00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:06.717
Success:

117
00:06:06.997 --> 00:06:08.149
Sample answers.

118
00:06:08.429 --> 00:06:16.109
Optimised 25 slow PostgreSQL queries, reducing report generation time from 40 s to 4 s.

119
00:06:16.389 --> 00:06:25.328
Migrated 8 services from on-premise servers to AWS ECS with zero downtime, cutting hosting costs by 30%.

120
00:06:26.678 --> 00:06:27.574
Part 9.

121
00:06:27.854 --> 00:06:28.899
Speak today.

122
00:06:30.149 --> 00:06:32.688
Rewrite your top 3 bullets using the formula.

123
00:06:32.968 --> 00:06:35.144
Shorten your summary to 2 to 3 lines.

124
00:06:35.424 --> 00:06:39.925
Explain your best bullet out loud in 30 seconds (it will come up in interviews).

125
00:06:41.275 --> 00:06:42.811
That's the end of this lesson.

126
00:06:43.091 --> 00:06:47.742
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

127
00:06:48.022 --> 00:06:54.145
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

